  "id": "RAW_ec7fd80fb8",
  "title": "超越编辑画布：OOXML 到 LLM 摄取中的证据分歧",
  "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880",
  "date": "2026-08-29 14:07:07",
  "author": "sbulaev",
  "siteName": "Hacker News - Newest: \"LLM\"",
  "content": "<!--\nrdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"\n         xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n         xmlns:trackback=\"http://madskills.com/public/xml/rss/module/trackback/\">\n    <rdf:Description\n        rdf:about=\"/abs/2608.25880\"\n        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2608.25880\"\n        dc:title=\"Beyond the Editing Canvas: Evidence Divergence in OOXML-to-LLM Ingestion\"\n        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2608.25880\" />\n    </rdf:RDF>\n-->\n<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div id=\"abs-outer\">\n   <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n    <div class=\"subheader\">\n     <h1>Computer Science &gt; Software Engineering</h1>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n     <strong>arXiv:2608.25880</strong> (cs)\n    </div>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n    <div id=\"content-inner\">\n     <div id=\"abs\">\n      <div class=\"dateline\">[Submitted on 26 Aug 2026]</div>\n      <div class=\"authors\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liu,+S\" rel=\"nofollow\">Side Liu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liu,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiangpeng Liu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xin,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jinwen Xin</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Peng,+G\" rel=\"nofollow\">Guojun Peng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ming,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiang Ming</a>\n      </div>\n      <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.25880\">View PDF</a> <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.25880v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n      <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>LLM pipelines increasingly ingest Office Open XML (OOXML) documents (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files) as first-class evidence in financial, compliance, and retrieval-augmented workflows, implicitly assuming semantic integrity: that the evidence consumed by the model matches the content shown in the Microsoft Office suite editing canvas. We show that this assumption can fail in OOXML-to-LLM pipelines. The same specification-valid OOXML file can yield one evidentiary view in Microsoft Office and another when extracted for an LLM. Each view is treated as authoritative by its consumer, a condition we call plural ground truth. The ingestion contract rarely states which view and semantic roles become model evidence or preserves how that evidence was derived. We call the specification-grounded OOXML constructions that induce such divergence evidence forks.\n       <br>\n       We systematically traverse and mine the OOXML specification and confirm 21 evidence forks across Excel, Word, and PowerPoint, spanning six dimensions of view construction. All 13 tools in our extraction panel emit evidence from at least one fork. We test four native-ingestion LLM APIs and seven web chatbots. Each test document carries a trap: a task-relevant fact exposed by extraction but not shown in Office. Across this 21-mechanism evaluation, the four APIs return the trap in 48--76% of trials. For 20 of 21 mechanisms, at least one of the eleven interfaces returns the trap. Our measurements further show that exposure is shaped upstream of the model by the ingestion path and extractor configuration. A source-level survey of sixteen popular open-source LLM projects further shows that default OOXML ingestion paths concentrate on affected extractor families.\n      </blockquote>\n      <!--CONTEXT-->\n      <div class=\"metatable\">\n       <table summary=\"Additional metadata\">\n        <tbody>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\"><span class=\"primary-subject\">Software Engineering (cs.SE)</span>; Cryptography and Security (cs.CR)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880\">arXiv:2608.25880</a> [cs.SE]</span></td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\"> <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880v1\">arXiv:2608.25880v1</a> [cs.SE]</span> for this version)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.25880\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.25880</a>\n           <div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n            <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\">\n              <path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h12v-64h-12c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h64c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v100h12c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v24z\" />\n             </svg>\n             <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Focus to learn more</span>\n            </button>\n            <!-- tooltip description -->\n            <div role=\"tooltip\" id=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <span class=\"left-corner\"></span> arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n            </div>\n           </div></td>\n         </tr>\n        </tbody>\n       </table>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"submission-history\">\n     <h2>Submission history</h2>\n     From: Side Liu [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/show-email/b41ebefb/2608.25880\" rel=\"nofollow\">view email</a>]\n     <br>\n     <strong>[v1]</strong> Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:52:44 UTC (361 KB)\n     <br>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end leftcolumn-->\n   <div class=\"extra-services\">\n    <div class=\"full-text\">\n     <a name=\"other\"></a> <span class=\"descriptor\">Full-text links:</span>\n     <h2>Access Paper:</h2>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.25880\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.25880v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/src/2608.25880\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source </a></li>\n     </ul>\n     <div class=\"abs-license\">\n      <a href=\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\">view license</a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <!--end full-text-->\n    <div class=\"browse\">\n     <h3 class=\"browse-context-heading\">Current browse context:</h3>\n     <div class=\"current\">cs.SE</div>\n     <div class=\"prevnext\">\n      <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button prev-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2608.25880&amp;function=prev&amp;context=cs.SE\" accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.SE (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a> </span> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">&nbsp; | &nbsp;</span> <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button next-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2608.25880&amp;function=next&amp;context=cs.SE\" accesskey=\"n\" title=\"next in cs.SE (accesskey n)\" rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a> </span>\n      <br>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"list\">\n      <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-new\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.SE/new\" rel=\"nofollow\">new</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-recent\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.SE/recent\" rel=\"nofollow\">recent</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-id\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.SE/2026-08\" rel=\"nofollow\">2026-08</a>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"abs-switch-cat\">\n      Change to browse by:\n      <div class=\"switch context-change\">\n       <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880?context=cs\" rel=\"nofollow\">cs</a>\n       <br class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">\n       <a class=\"subclass\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880?context=cs.CR\" rel=\"nofollow\">cs.CR</a>\n       <br class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <h3>References &amp; Citations</h3>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-ads\" href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2608.25880\">NASA ADS</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-google-scholar\" href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=2608.25880\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Google Scholar</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-semantic-scholar\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:2608.25880\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Semantic Scholar</a></li>\n     </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <button type=\"button\" id=\"bib-cite-trigger\" class=\"bib-cite-button abs-button\">export BibTeX citation</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bookmarks\">\n     <div>\n      <h3>Bookmark</h3>\n     </div>\n     <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&amp;url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880&amp;description=Beyond the Editing Canvas: Evidence Divergence in OOXML-to-LLM Ingestion\" title=\"Bookmark on BibSonomy\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/bibsonomy.png\" alt=\"BibSonomy\"> </a> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25880&amp;title=Beyond the Editing Canvas: Evidence Divergence in OOXML-to-LLM Ingestion\" title=\"Bookmark on Reddit\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/reddit.png\" alt=\"Reddit\"> </a>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end extra-services-->\n   <!-- LABS AREA -->\n   <div id=\"labstabs\"></div>\n   <!-- END LABS AREA -->\n   <div class=\"endorsers\">\n    <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/auth/show-endorsers/2608.25880\" class=\"endorser-who\" rel=\"nofollow\">Which authors of this paper are endorsers?</a> | Disable MathJax (<a href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/mathjax.html\">What is MathJax?</a>) <span class=\"help\" style=\"font-style: normal; float: right; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 1em;\"></span>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "本文揭示，同一个 OOXML 文件可以为 Microsoft Office 和 LLM 管道生成不同的证据视图，导致“多元地面真理”和潜在的 AI 工作流数据完整性问题。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "本文揭示，同一个 OOXML 文件可以为 Microsoft Office 和 LLM 管道生成不同的证据视图，导致“多元地面真理”和潜在的 AI 工作流数据完整性问题。",
  "summary": "该研究质疑了 LLM 从 OOXML 文件中摄取的内容与 Microsoft Office 显示内容一致的假设。它识别出 21 个“证据分叉”，即文件结构允许存在分歧的解读，导致模型看到编辑画布中不可见的隐藏信息。这种分歧威胁到用于文档分析的 AI 系统的可靠性。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "多元地面真理",
      "explanation": "同一个 OOXML 文件可以生成两种截然不同的权威数据视图：一种用于 Office 中的人类编辑，另一种用于 LLM 管道中的机器。这导致文档的“真理”取决于其消费上下文。"
    },
    {
      "point": "证据分叉",
      "explanation": "研究识别了 OOXML 规范中的特定构造，这些构造允许这种分歧。这意味着 LLM 可能会分析用户未察觉的隐藏或替代数据表示。"
    },
    {
      "point": "管道脆弱性",
      "explanation": "这种分歧并非理论上的，而是当前系统中实际存在的。论文证明，流行的提取工具和 LLM API 经常返回“分叉”数据，导致基于不完整或误导信息的决策存在错误风险。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "{\"quote\":\"同一个规范有效的 OOXML 文件可以在 Microsoft Office 中产生一种证据视图，而在提取用于 LLM 时产生另一种视图。\"，\"attribution\":\"论文\"}",
    "{\"quote\":\"我们将这些导致分歧的规范基础 OOXML 构造称为证据分叉。\"，\"attribution\":\"论文\"}",
    "{\"quote\":\"摄取合约很少说明哪些视图和语义角色成为模型证据，或者如何保留这些证据的来源。\"，\"attribution\":\"论文\"}"
  ],
